// ─── SEED EXTENSION 2026-07-11 — thermodynamic efficiency programme ─────────
// Source: DS theory corpus (seven_ideas_deep.vsm idea 2, viable_compressor.vsm
// VC-2) as corrected by Claude review (claude_review_seven_ideas.vsm §3, §4).
// This extension folds the "kernel as thermal engine" idea into P3, which is
// its natural home (Maxwell Demon → Landauer → Lindblad).

thermodynamic_efficiency: {
  claim:
    "The VSF kernel is a cybernetic regulator whose efficiency can be measured
     as two SEPARATE ratios — never a composite:
       η₁ = decision bits emitted / variety bits ingested   (Ashby ratio)
       η₂ = decision bits emitted / joules dissipated       (Landauer ratio)
     These would be the first published efficiency baselines for a running
     cybernetic regulator."

  methodology_lock:
    "Dissipation = electrical power drawn (RAPL counters), NEVER ΔT×C_thermal
     (that is stored energy, not dissipated power — review §4.idea_2).
     Landauer PROXIMITY must not be claimed: silicon dissipates 10⁸-10⁹ × kT·ln2
     per operation; the interesting number is the baseline, not the distance
     to a limit no CMOS device approaches."

  core_citation:
    "Still, Sivak, Bell & Crooks (2012), 'Thermodynamics of Prediction',
     PRL 109, 120604 — dissipation = useless nostalgia: a predictor's
     thermodynamic inefficiency equals the information it retains about the
     past that does not help predict the future. This upgrades the Landauer
     framing to a MEASURABLE claim on our kernel: V_mem retention vs its
     predictive value for the next-tick state. If V_mem stores more history
     than it uses predictively, that excess is (by Still et al.) a lower
     bound on avoidable dissipation. No one has run this test on a
     production control kernel."

  soplo_as_demon:
    "EXP-SOPLO-01 (spec exists) makes the φ↑ filter the demon: it passes
     low-entropy (viable) signals and blocks high-entropy variety. The
     measurement cost of the sorting is the kernel's CPU time — the demon's
     Landauer bill, paid in watts we can meter. Complements the S4-as-
     measurement-apparatus mapping above: S4 is the demon at the deliberative
     layer, the soplo is the demon at the reflex layer."

  autopoietic_interpretation:
    "PREDICTION: η₁ will be low and stable. A viable system spends most of
     its variety-processing on structural self-maintenance (Merkle chain,
     Lyapunov tracking, V_mem) and only a small surplus on external decisions.
     A low η is EVIDENCE FOR the self-maintenance reading, not a failure of
     regulation — the system's primary product is itself. Frame inconvenient
     numbers this way honestly: the finding is the profile Δη under load,
     not the absolute value."

  data_dependency:
    "Task AC-ETA-MEASURE (TASKS.vsm, agent=[S]) produces η₁/η₂ first for the
     AC paper's Limitations upgrade; P3 inherits those numbers and extends to
     the three-regime profile (idle / thermal / LLM-loaded) + the Still test."
}
